{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Cancel Effects"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","type":"reference"},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" effect or the imperative ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" method. Identity lives outside the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancel id is any "},{"code":"Hashable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"code":"cancelInFlight: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"type":"text","text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","type":"heading","text":"What it does not replace"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"code":"defer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.cancel(id:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancellable"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"cancelInFlight","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","text":"Effect"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleff